{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1829318","formula":"C₁₉H₂₀N₂O₃","hill":"C19H20N2O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"H":20.0,"N":2.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Dolasetron","ru":"Доласетрон"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dolasetron (trade name Anzemet) is a serotonin 5-HT3 receptor antagonist used to treat nausea and vomiting following chemotherapy. Its main effect is to reduce the activity of the vagus nerve, which is a nerve that activates the vomiting center in the medulla oblongata. It does not have much antiemetic effect when symptoms are due to motion sickness.","ru":"Доласетрон (англ. Dolasetron) — лекарственное средство, которое используется для предотвращения тошноты и рвоты, связанных с цитотоксическими эффектами химиотерапии. Доласетрон назначается в виде таблеток или инъекций."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":60654,"mass":324.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1[C@@H]2CC(CC3N2CC(=O)C1C3)OC(=O)C4=CNC5=CC=CC=C54","inchikey":"UKTAZPQNNNJVKR-DBBXXEFVSA-N","iupac":"[(7R)-10-oxo-8-azatricyclo[5.3.1.03,8]undecan-5-yl] 1H-indole-3-carboxylate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"60654","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.335,"y":0.882,"z":0.205,"el":"O"},{"x":-6.738,"y":-0.84,"z":0.077,"el":"O"},{"x":1.049,"y":-1.305,"z":0.292,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.623,"y":0.558,"z":-1.044,"el":"N"},{"x":4.218,"y":1.939,"z":-0.12,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.411,"y":1.34,"z":0.202,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.89,"y":-0.731,"z":-0.939,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.507,"y":-0.787,"z":0.995,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.962,"y":0.576,"z":1.433,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.422,"y":-1.573,"z":0.25,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.921,"y":1.693,"z":0.341,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.38,"y":-0.458,"z":-0.843,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.019,"y":0.46,"z":0.324,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.068,"y":0.3,"z":-1.236,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.57,"y":-0.484,"z":-0.04,"el":"C"},{"x":1.27,"y":-0.107